# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line endings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. Every generator in scripts/ writes with newline="\n",
# deliberately, so its output is byte-identical on any platform. Without this
# file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what is set here)
# materialises those same files as CRLF on checkout. Regenerating one then
# rewrites it as LF, and `git status` reports a modification whose content is
# identical to HEAD.
#
# That is not cosmetic. The clean-checkout run on 2026-08-15 regenerated all six
# tables and both CSVs; every one matched its committed blob byte for byte, and
# git listed all six tables as modified anyway. A REAL change would have looked
# exactly the same, so the noise was hiding the signal in the one check that
# exists to detect drift.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the checkout match what the generators write, so a
# modification shown by git is a modification in fact.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Generated and hand-maintained text. The four extensions cover every generated
# output in the repository: tables/*.tex, notes/*.md and figures/README.md,
# data/*.csv, and every runs/*/config.json.
*.tex   text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Not listed above and deliberately so: *.py and *.ps1 are not generated, and
# *.pdf / *.png are binary and must never be touched by an eol filter.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.zip   binary
